    files and nothing sherpa-related.
  - apps/server-core/Dockerfile's runtime stage installs only socket.io by
    default; sherpa-onnx-node is NOT installed unless a self-hoster opts in
    manually (the Dockerfile says so in its own header comment).
`sherpa-onnx-node` is a real optionalDependency of apps/server-core
though (package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml), so anyone building the open-source
tree from source with `pnpm install` does pull it from the public npm
registry — this section exists for that case, and in case the native-
binary staging gap above ever gets closed in a later round.

